        "546ecfee-021a-42ea-9860-5d2d93c0a8e2": {
            "type": "multicolumn",
            "blocks": {
                "d427cc04-05a2-46d9-8f00-efe4ec026c14": {
                    "type": "column",
                    "settings": {
                        "image": "shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Frame_2.png",
                        "title": "Moringa Leaf (Moringa oleifera)",
                        "text": "<p>Packed with essential nutrients like vitamins A, C, and E, this herbal galactagogue has been shown to increase breast milk levels by 47%, according to a 2022 study. The same study found that the exclusive breastfeeding rate at 6 months was 52.3% in the group of mothers who’d taken Moringa oleifera. For context, the percentage of infants born in 2020 in the U.S. who were breastfed exclusively through 6 months was 25.4%, according to the National Immunization Survey.<\/p><h6>Source: Fungtammasan S and Phupong V. <a href=\"https:\/\/www.sciencedirect.com\/science\/article\/pii\/S2590161322000321?via%3Dihub\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">The effect of Moringa oleifera capsule in increasing breast milk volume in early postpartum patients: A double-blind, randomized controlled trial<\/span><\/a>. Eur J Obstet Gynecol Reprod Biol X. 2022 Dec; 16: 100171. DOI: 10.1016\/j.eurox.2022.100171<\/h6>",
                        "link_label": "",
                        "link": ""
                    }
                },
                "template--18907466105126__546ecfee-021a-42ea-9860-5d2d93c0a8e2-column-1": {
                    "type": "column",
                    "settings": {
                        "image": "shopify:\/\/shop_images\/founded.png",
                        "title": "Goat’s Rue (Galega officinalis)",
                        "text": "<p>A popular herbal galactagogue that won’t leave its usual bitter taste in your mouth from our formula. While you most likely know of Goat’s Rue through friends who tried it for boosting milk supply, it's also got street cred. A <a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/27901335\/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">survey<\/span><\/a> found that of 238 mothers using a goat's rue supplement, 67% felt they had an increase in milk production and 88% felt that the product had benefited their breastfeeding experience.<\/p><h6>Source: Salatino S, Giacomelli L, Carnevali I, et al. <a href=\"https:\/\/pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/27901335\/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">The role of natural galactagogues during breastfeeding. Focus on a Galega officinalis based food supplement<\/span><\/a>. Minerva Pediatr. 2017;69:531–7. DOI: 10.23736\/S0026-4946.16.04797-6<\/h6>",
                        "link_label": "",
                        "link": ""
                    }
                },
